course: dictionary
lesson: 10226
title: The toaster: heat and safety
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A toaster is a small electric machine that browns slices of bread by heating them. Its name is a clue: it toasts. Notice the word electric too, because electricity is what makes it work and what can hurt you.
explain: «You must never poke a knife or fork into a toaster, even when it is switched off at the wall.» The word never is a strong warning. Metal can carry electricity, so putting it inside can give you a shock.
explain: If bread gets stuck, do not reach in with anything. Unplug the toaster first, let it cool, and ask an adult. «Putting metal into a toaster while it is plugged in can give you an electric shock.» Those two sentences give you the safe rule.
fact: A toaster is a small electric kitchen machine that browns slices of bread by heating them.
fact: The plural of toaster is toasters. You might also hear pop up from the toaster or toaster oven.
fact: The wires in a toaster glow red because electricity makes them hot.
fact: «Putting metal into a toaster while it is plugged in can give you an electric shock.»
fact: «Old crumbs in a toaster can catch fire, so a grown-up empties the crumb tray when it is unplugged and cold.»
exercise: What is a toaster? | *A small electric kitchen machine that browns slices of bread by heating them | A kind of oven that cooks whole meals | A tool for cutting bread into thin slices | A cupboard where bread is kept fresh
exercise: «You must never poke a knife or fork into a toaster, even when it is switched off at the wall.» Why? | *Metal can give you an electric shock | Forks make the bread taste better | The toaster needs metal to pop up | It stops the crumbs from falling out
exercise: Why do the wires in a toaster glow red? | Because bread makes them shine | Because the toaster is painted red | *Because electricity makes them hot | Because they are made of glass
test: If bread gets stuck in a toaster, what should you do first? | Poke it out with a fork | *Unplug it and ask an adult | Shake the toaster hard | Pour water on it to cool it
test: Why does a grown-up empty the crumb tray? | To keep the crumbs for a cake | Because crumbs make the bread brown | *Because old crumbs can catch fire | To make the toaster lighter
exam: Which is a safe rule for a toaster? | *Keep it away from water and do not leave it on unattended | Leave it on all night so it is ready | Put metal in it while it is plugged in | Keep it near water so it stays cool
